    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-textus</span></b> , a, um,
		Part. [texo], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>woven all around</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">velamen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 1, 649</span></i>
			. —<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-textum</span></b> , i, n.,
				<i>a garment inwoven with purple</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et quod amictui habet purpuram circum, vocant
					circumtextum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 132</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 19, 24,
		10</span></i>.</div>
